  "summary": "W42 accounts the live creature and item cache tables, queued requests, item fingerprints, and pending fill inputs. It verifies that application, icon and content preview references share the creature renderer and that the two item routes share one item renderer. The report covers their direct table allocations, cube and scratch uploads, persistent targets, and item surface upload records. Borrowed skin textures remain with their source. Fallback item textures use at most the six existing colors. Failed target replacements preserve the previous attachments and refused surface uploads retire provisional buffers. All 46 Release regression groups, eight related tests and scoped native checks pass. Shared asset payloads, external filesystem, CRT, decoder stack, driver and whole-process costs and full S0–S6 acceptance remain open.",
